WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
Heat some blue copper
sulfate crystals,

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.530
and they crumble into a white
powder as water is driven off.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.830
Now add a few drops of
water to that white powder.

4
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.710
It turns blue again.

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.190
So can a chemical reaction
really run backwards?

6
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.830
And if it can, does it ever finish?

7
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.970
In this mission, you'll
meet reversible reactions,

8
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.480
and the special arrow that shows
a reaction can go both ways.

9
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:28.070
You'll find out what dynamic
equilibrium means in a closed

10
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.810
system, and see how changing
the conditions can shift it one

11
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.390
way or the other.

12
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.950
Your mission: find out whether
a reversible reaction ever

13
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.180
finishes.
